 "version": 1,
 "title": "Electro Beat",
 "category": "Drums and grooves",
 "text": "Sound: an early-80s electro and hip-hop machine beat: a punchy, syncopated kick, a snappy snare on 2 and 4, ticking sixteenth hats and a cowbell. It plays by itself.\n\nHow it's built: one Clock at 112. Three Sequencers on eighths: the kick (steps 1, 4 and 7), the snare (3 and 7), the cowbell (2, 6 and 8). The cowbell is two pulse waves a sixth apart through a band-pass, struck by a short envelope. Hats on every 1/16.\n\nTweak: the kick and cowbell steps, the cowbell oscillators' TUNE, TEMPO.",
